    "answer": {
      "short": "$y = 2$ when $x = 2$ is incorrect; it should be $1$.",
      "worked": "Check each value of $x$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}x=-1:\\ 5-2(-1)&=7\\\\x=0:\\ 5-2(0)&=5\\\\x=1:\\ 5-2(1)&=3\\\\x=2:\\ 5-2(2)&=1\\\\x=3:\\ 5-2(3)&=-1\\end{aligned}$$\nWhen $x = 2$, $y = 1$, not $2$. So the value $y = 2$ is incorrect.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
